WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:11.380
44. What are carbon offsets? As the idea of global warming gains more acceptance in

2
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:17.660
the world, scientists are scrambling for a way to stop it before it's too late. One of

3
00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:25.180
these ways is by using carbon offsets, also called carbon sharing. Carbon offsets were

4
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:31.220
designed to help countries comply with their obligations under the Kyoto Protocol. Under

5
00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:37.800
the Kyoto Protocol, countries agree to reduce their carbon emissions by a certain percent.

6
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:43.900
Carbon emissions are measured in tons of carbon dioxide or other greenhouse gases. But because

7
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:50.140
these countries only have to reduce their total emissions, not every business or organization,

8
00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:55.420
or even every country, has to reduce their emissions by the same amount. They just have

9
00:00:55.460 --> 00:01:02.380
to reach the correct total reduction. Some countries, companies, and organizations can

10
00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:08.620
reduce their carbon emissions more easily than others. Carbon offsets allow them to sell these

11
00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:15.180
reductions to other entities that are moving more slowly. So a country or company can buy

12
00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:21.260
carbon credits somewhere else. This prevents carbon from being emitted somewhere, but not by

13
00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:27.340
that particular entity. Carbon offsets are controversial because they allow polluters to

14
00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:34.260
avoid reducing their own carbon emissions. I won't turn off my tap. I'll pay someone else 10 pounds

15
00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:40.140
to pay someone else 2 pounds to turn off their own tap, explain members of the environmental

16
00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:47.100
group Rising Tide, which opposes carbon offsets. Others, however, say that carbon offsets are a

17
00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:52.740
good way to reduce emissions overall while big countries figure out how to cut their own

18
00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:59.260
emissions without hurting their economies. As the Kyoto Protocol is enforced and the world

19
00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:05.500
becomes more serious about greenhouse gas reductions, carbon offset programs will become

20
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:12.660
widespread. Understanding this complex issue is very important if you want to stop global warming.

21
00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:19.660
Keep researching and decide for yourself if selling carbon offsets will help or hurt us all.
